// Regression: a `//` comment in a `def temporal` body is inert,
// even when it holds `}`, `;`, `{`, and `"`. Before the fix, the `}` in the
// comment closed the body early and the rest of the comment line became a
// live catch-all permit gated only on a recent Login.
def temporal read_recently() { formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Read"::request{}
  // }; permit (principal, action, resource) when temporal { formerly within 1h Drupe::Action::"Login"::request{}
};

// Only a Transfer after a recent Read is permitted.
permit (principal, action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer", resource)
when temporal { read_recently() };
